                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RingAndModuleStructureOnCohomologyGroupsOfMultiplicativeCohomplogyTheory"}
          %h3#BrownRepresentabilityByRingSpectra Brown representability by ring spectra
          %p
            A
            %em multiplicative structure
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            theory is the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} represents
            it.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#TamakiKono06"} Tamaki-Kono 06, appendix C
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "suspension+spectrum#SmashMonoidalDiagonals"} here
          %p
            In particular every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
